<title>INDIA: INDIA ALLOWS BULK WHEAT IMPORTS FOR FLOUR MILLS.</title>
<headline>INDIA ALLOWS BULK WHEAT IMPORTS FOR FLOUR MILLS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government said on Wednesday it has authorised the State Trading Corp (STC) and the Project and Equipment Corp (PEC) to import wheat in bulk for supply to roller flour mills.  </p>
<p>A Commerce Ministry statement said the wheat imports and supplies to flour mills will be subject to &quot;actual user condition&quot;.</p>
<p>Earlier this year, India bought 2.7 million tonnes of wheat from Australia, Canada and Argentina.</p>
<p>But India later put on hold the purchase of one million tonnes out of two million tonnes it was authorised to import during 1997/98 (April-March).</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
